<!-- MAIN CONTENT --><section><strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-ansi-language:EN;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA'><br
clear=all style='mso-special-character:line-break;page-break-before:always'>
</span></strong>

<p class=MsoNormal><strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-ansi-language:
EN'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></strong></p>

<div>

<div>

<div>

<p style='background:#E8F0F7'><b><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:#1F4E78;mso-ansi-language:EN'>Project
Overview:</span></b><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN'> The Canadian <span class=SpellE>ThermoCHronology</span>
(CATCH) database is a $400,000 CAD national platform integrating 51 years of
thermochronology data. Developed by Lithodat for Natural Resources Canada's
Geological Survey, CATCH demonstrates direct alignment with GDAC-SA
requirements through proven capability in multi-decade data integration, legacy
data digitization, and FAIR-compliant national database architecture delivered
on-time and on-budget. <o:p></o:p></span></p>

</div>

<div style='mso-element:para-border-div;border:none;border-bottom:solid #1F4E78 1.5pt;
padding:0cm 0cm 4.0pt 0cm'>

<h2><span lang=EN style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-ansi-language:EN'>1. Overview<o:p></o:p></span></h2>

</div>

<p><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN'>The CATCH database is Canada's first unified
national repository for <span class=GramE>low-temperature</span>
thermochronology data, integrating 1,427 samples from 91 publications spanning
1970-2021. Developed by Lithodat Pty Ltd (Fabian Kohlmann, Malcolm McMillan)
with the Geological Survey of Canada (Dr. Jeremy Powell, Dr. Dawn Kellett),
CATCH demonstrates national-scale data standardization directly applicable to
GDAC-SA's multi-agency integration requirements.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN'>Performance:</span></strong><span lang=EN
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black;mso-ansi-language:
EN'> $400,000 CAD, 18 months (October 2021 - March 2023), delivered on-time and
on-budget. Platform scale: 996 fission-track datapoints, 762 (U-Th)/He
datapoints, 16,277 single grain measurements, published via DOI
10.4095/pdreqf905k and accessible through AusGeochem.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<div style='mso-element:para-border-div;border:none;border-bottom:solid #1F4E78 1.5pt;
padding:0cm 0cm 4.0pt 0cm'>

<h2><span lang=EN style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-ansi-language:EN'>2. History &amp; Funding<o:p></o:p></span></h2>

</div>

<p><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN'>Natural Resources Canada's Geological Survey
(GSC) is Canada's national geoscience organization. Prior to CATCH, Canada had
no central thermochronology database despite decades of published
research—analogous to GDAC-SA's challenge of fragmented geological survey data.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN'>In October 2021, GSC awarded Lithodat a
$400,000 CAD contract to design Canada's first national thermochronology data
model, harvest all published research (1970-2021), and integrate with <span
class=SpellE>AusGeochem's</span> FAIR platform. The project required systematic
harmonization of legacy laboratory outputs from multiple provinces, automated
QA/QC pipeline development, and extensive legacy data digitization from
analogue paper reports and non-vectorized PDFs.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN'>Deliverables included national data schema
accommodating four <span class=SpellE>thermochronometer</span> types
(apatite/zircon fission-track, apatite/zircon (U-Th)/He), standardization of 51
years of provincial data, complete harvesting from 91 publications, and
integration with international reporting standards.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<div style='mso-element:para-border-div;border:none;border-bottom:solid #1F4E78 1.5pt;
padding:0cm 0cm 4.0pt 0cm'>

<h2><span lang=EN style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-ansi-language:EN'>3. Key Collaborators<o:p></o:p></span></h2>

</div>

<p><strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN'>Client:</span></strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:
11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN'>
Natural Resources Canada - Geological Survey of Canada (equivalent to Saudi
Geological Survey).<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN'>Project Leadership:</span></strong><span lang=EN
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black;mso-ansi-language:
EN'> Dr. Jeremy Powell (GSC project lead, first author), Dr. Dawn Kellett (GSC
co-author), demonstrating government partnership excellence.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN'>Provincial Integration:</span></strong><span lang=EN
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black;mso-ansi-language:
EN'> All Canadian provincial geological surveys contributed data requiring
standardization across boundaries—demonstrating multi-agency harmonization
applicable to GDAC-SA.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN'>Platform:</span></strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:
11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN'>
AusGeochem provides FAIR data access, enabling international research community
access through open-source platform.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<div style='mso-element:para-border-div;border:none;border-bottom:solid #1F4E78 1.5pt;
padding:0cm 0cm 4.0pt 0cm'>

<h2><span lang=EN style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-ansi-language:EN'>4. Platform Capabilities<o:p></o:p></span></h2>

</div>

<p><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN'>CATCH employs purpose-built data structure
accommodating four <span class=SpellE>thermochronometer</span> types
(Apatite/Zircon Fission Track, Apatite/Zircon (U-Th)/He) plus thermal history
modeling. Canada's first unified national thermochronology schema handles
complex kinetic parameters, accommodates legacy laboratory outputs, and
provides ML-compatible, cloud-ready structure.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<div>

<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN;
mso-no-proof:yes'><!--[if gte vml 1]><v:shape id="Picture_x0020_3" o:spid="_x0000_i1025"
 type="#_x0000_t75" alt="CATCH database northern Canada compilation map"
 style='width:442pt;height:261pt;visibility:visible;mso-wrap-style:square'>
 <v:imagedata src="I-NRCan-Project-Summary-Clean.fld/image003.png" o:title="CATCH database northern Canada compilation map"/>
</v:shape><![endif]--><![if !vml]><img width=442 height=261
src="I-NRCan-Project-Summary-Clean.fld/image003.png"
alt="CATCH database northern Canada compilation map" v:shapes="Picture_x0020_3"><![endif]></span><span
lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman";color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN'><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<div>

<p class=MsoNormal><strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-ansi-language:
EN'>Figure 1:</span></strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";color:black;
mso-ansi-language:EN'> CATCH database northern Canada compilation showing 1,427
sample locations with <span class=GramE>low-temperature</span> thermochronology
data (colored by geologic age: red = Precambrian, green = Paleozoic, blue =
Mesozoic, yellow = Cenozoic). Demonstrates national-scale geospatial data
integration with complete metadata capture for 51 years of published research.
Data accessible via AusGeochem platform. <o:p></o:p></span></p>

</div>

</div>

<p><strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN'>Advanced Features:</span></strong><span lang=EN
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black;mso-ansi-language:
EN'> Single grain data preservation (16,277 measurements), fission-track length
capture (27,848 measurements) from digitized histograms, automated QA/QC
pipelines validated by GSC scientists, comprehensive provenance tracking,
georeferencing workflow, and thermal history modeling integration.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<div style='mso-element:para-border-div;border:none;border-bottom:solid #1F4E78 1.5pt;
padding:0cm 0cm 4.0pt 0cm'>

<h2><span lang=EN style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-ansi-language:EN'>5. FAIR Data &amp; Project Performance<o:p></o:p></span></h2>

</div>

<p><strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN'>FAIR Principles:</span></strong><span lang=EN
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black;mso-ansi-language:
EN'> Findable via DOI (10.4095/pdreqf905k) in GSC Open File series; Accessible
through AusGeochem platform with no authentication barriers; Interoperable
using community-agreed schemas; Reusable with complete metadata and
ML-compatible structure.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN'>On-Time, On-Budget:</span></strong><span lang=EN
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black;mso-ansi-language:
EN'> 18-month timeline met (October 2021 - March 2023), $400,000 CAD managed
with complete accountability, demonstrating reliable government partnership.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN'>National-Scale Achievement:</span></strong><span lang=EN
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black;mso-ansi-language:
EN'> Standardized data across entire Canadian territory, harmonized provincial
inconsistencies, integrated 51 years of data (1970-2021), harvested all
published research from 91 sources—demonstrating systematic multi-decade
integration applicable to GDAC-SA.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN'>Technical Excellence:</span></strong><span lang=EN
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black;mso-ansi-language:
EN'> Automated data ingestion for multiple formats (digital, analogue paper,
non-vectorized PDFs), QA/QC validation by GSC staff, and cloud-ready
infrastructure supporting advanced analytics.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<div style='mso-element:para-border-div;border:none;border-bottom:solid #1F4E78 1.5pt;
padding:0cm 0cm 4.0pt 0cm'>

<h2><span lang=EN style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-ansi-language:EN'>6. Publications &amp; Recognition<o:p></o:p></span></h2>

</div>

<p><strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN'>Powell, J.W., Kellett, D.A., Kohlmann, F., and McMillan,
M. (2025).</span></strong><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN'> Canadian <span
class=SpellE>ThermoCHronology</span> (CATCH) database: northern Canada
compilation. <em><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Geological Survey
of Canada, Open File 9225</span></em>, 1 .zip file. DOI: <a
href="https://doi.org/10.4095/pdreqf905k">10.4095/pdreqf905k</a><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><em><span lang=EN style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN'>Official government publication documenting
Lithodat's design of Canada's first unified thermochronology data model and
curation of 51 years of legacy data. Demonstrates multi-format extraction
pipelines, automated QA/QC frameworks, and FAIR data implementation at national
scale. The project's scope and methodologies are directly transferable to
GDAC-SA's requirements for integrating historical geological survey data with
modern analytics infrastructure.</span></em><span lang=EN style='font-size:
11.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN'><o:p></o:p></span></p>

